    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="1040" n="912" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg912"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/148</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1928-07-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received
                        August 9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1798</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s confidential
                    instruction No. 1017 of June 21st last regarding the proposed new reconstruction
                    loan to Austria,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d775-f1"/> I have the honor to report
                    that in the course of a conversation at the Foreign Office to-day with
                    Undersecretary Grandi, he informed me that there had been no change in the
                    Italian Government’s attitude with regard to this matter, as expressed to the
                    Department by the Italian Ambassador.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d775-f1" n="58" xml:id="d775-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see similar instruction to Minister in Austria, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
